<h1>Measure_Plane</h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p class="description"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> Calls a wizard for capture/scan datum plane using the localiser probe/sensor.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Parameters</b></span>:</p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span style="font-style:italic; font-weight:bold;"><i><b>Name</b></i></span> – name of the resulting datum plane that will be created.</p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span style="font-style:italic; font-weight:bold;"><i><b>Prompt</b></i></span> – text to be used on the first step of the wizard: Available values are:</p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">Empty string ( <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>""</i></span> ) – wizard should display the default text.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">Non-empty string – wizard should use this string.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span style="font-style:italic; font-weight:bold;"><i><b>Method</b></i></span> – determines measurement method. Available values are:</p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span style="font-style:italic;"><i>Capture</i></span> – uses probe to measure the datum plane.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span style="font-style:italic;"><i>Scan</i></span> – uses scanning to measure the datum plane. When this value is used <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>MaxPoints</i></span> parameter is ignored.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span style="font-style:italic; font-weight:bold;"><i><b>ImmediateAccept</b></i></span> – determines the behaviour of the wizard when finish. Available values are:</p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span style="font-style:italic;"><i>Yes</i></span> – when finish capture the datum plane will be created silently, i.e. no Accept/Reject dialog.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span style="font-style:italic;"><i>No</i></span> – when finish capture Accept/Reject dialog with the results should be displayed and user could select whether to accept or reject the plane.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span style="font-style:italic; font-weight:bold;"><i><b>MaxPoints</b></i></span> – limits number of the points that should be captured for the plane. If it is zero number of points is unlimited, i.e. default behaviour of the wizard. If it is higher than zero then when last point is captured wizard finishes automatically, i.e. without pressing Finish button. Accept/Reject dialog appears optionally – depending on the value of <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>ImmediateAccept</i></span> parameter. Minimum number of points for plane is 3.</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>UI Commands</b></span>:</p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span><i style="font-style:italic;">Datum &gt; Plane</i></span> from the localiser driven menu<span style="font-style:italic;"><i>.</i></span></p>
<p class="Warning">'Out of tolerance' option from <span style="font-style:italic;"><i>System &gt; Preferences &gt; Datum Capture</i></span> dialog applies (if enabled) when the plane is captured via macro command. ‘Continue capturing (Yes/No)’ dialog is not displayed. Wizard is terminated when finish capture and optionally accept/reject entity.</p>
<p class="ExampleCode">Example:</p>
<p class="ExampleCode">Measure_Plane( Name="Plane 1", Prompt="Capture Plane 1", Method="Capture", ImmediateAccept=Yes, MaxPoints=0 )</p>
